1
00:00:42,073 --> 00:00:46,068
MY ROYAL NEMESIS

2
00:00:49,071 --> 00:00:49,946
<i>Hello?</i>

3
00:00:50,030 --> 00:00:51,531
Where's Shin Seo-ri? Is she with you?

4
00:00:51,615 --> 00:00:53,325
Wait, didn't she go to see you?

5
00:00:53,408 --> 00:00:55,285
<i>They said she left</i>
<i>after her boyfriend called.</i>

6
00:00:55,369 --> 00:00:57,120
-Who said that?
-It wasn't a crew member.

7
00:00:57,204 --> 00:00:59,039
I think it was an extra.

8
00:01:00,248 --> 00:01:01,583
Damn it.

9
00:01:06,004 --> 00:01:07,089
Shin Seo-ri.

10
00:01:09,633 --> 00:01:11,134
Shin Seo-ri, wake up.

11
00:01:11,635 --> 00:01:12,969
Shin Seo-ri.

12
00:01:13,470 --> 00:01:14,471
Shin Seo-ri!

13
00:01:25,357 --> 00:01:26,441
You're okay.

14
00:01:27,776 --> 00:01:28,985
You're okay.

15
00:01:31,988 --> 00:01:33,198
Shin Seo-ri, look at me.

16
00:01:34,157 --> 00:01:35,659
I'm right here.

17
00:01:37,661 --> 00:01:38,787
Who do you think you are?

18
00:01:39,746 --> 00:01:41,206
Who are you to…

19
00:01:48,171 --> 00:01:49,798
What am I supposed to do?

20
00:01:52,342 --> 00:01:54,594
What do you want from me?

21
00:02:17,651 --> 00:02:21,940
EPISODE 12
RECLAIMING LOST TIME

22
00:02:22,080 --> 00:02:23,498
She's on her way home?

23
00:02:23,582 --> 00:02:24,916
I mean…

24
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,084
Hello?

25
00:02:27,294 --> 00:02:28,628
You couldn't tell me any sooner?

26
00:02:28,712 --> 00:02:30,797
Got me running around in circles.

27
00:02:37,429 --> 00:02:39,890
GONG TAE-WOO AND HAN MIN-HUI EXPECTING

28
00:02:39,973 --> 00:02:41,266
Damn it.

29
00:02:42,517 --> 00:02:44,895
Gong Tae-woo, that bastard.

30
00:02:44,978 --> 00:02:46,104
So much for "anti-marriage."

31
00:02:46,188 --> 00:02:49,357
It hasn't even been two months
since we broke up.

32
00:02:49,441 --> 00:02:50,859
And you got her pregnant?

33
00:03:04,706 --> 00:03:05,916
Ji-hyo.

34
00:03:05,999 --> 00:03:06,917
What?

35
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:10,212
You have a morning shoot tomorrow.
You shouldn't be doing all this right now.

36
00:03:10,295 --> 00:03:13,089
Baek Gwang-nam?
Shouldn't you be following Shin Seo-ri?

37
00:03:13,173 --> 00:03:15,217
How did you end up here?

38
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:16,676
Did you put a GPS on me?

39
00:03:18,136 --> 00:03:20,096
You're a celebrity, so act like one.

40
00:03:20,180 --> 00:03:21,515
Have some composure.

41
00:03:21,598 --> 00:03:23,266
Maintain some basic etiquette.

42
00:03:23,350 --> 00:03:25,227
Etiquette, my ass.

43
00:03:25,727 --> 00:03:27,145
Why don't you show some?

44
00:03:27,229 --> 00:03:30,565
I mean, if you're a manager,
you should act like one.

45
00:03:30,649 --> 00:03:32,442
You always talk back.

46
00:03:32,526 --> 00:03:34,611
What, are you…

47
00:03:34,694 --> 00:03:35,987
rich or something?

48
00:03:36,571 --> 00:03:38,156
What are you talking about? Jeez.

49
00:03:38,949 --> 00:03:40,367
Why did you take your socks off?

50
00:03:40,450 --> 00:03:42,285
Gong Tae-woo, I hope you go bald.

51
00:03:42,369 --> 00:03:43,578
Shiny bald head.

52
00:03:43,662 --> 00:03:46,581
Ji-hyo, please get up. Come on.

53
00:03:46,665 --> 00:03:47,624
Let go.

54
00:03:47,707 --> 00:03:49,376
Go sleep at home. Get up. Please.

55
00:03:49,459 --> 00:03:51,503
I live here.

56
00:03:51,586 --> 00:03:52,546
Let me take you home.

57
00:03:52,629 --> 00:03:54,339
I told you I'm buying today.

58
00:03:54,840 --> 00:03:56,007
-Who are you?
-Jeez.

59
00:03:56,091 --> 00:03:57,551
-Hold on.
-Wrong room, I guess.

60
00:04:01,221 --> 00:04:02,347
-Wait.
-What are you doing?

61
00:04:02,430 --> 00:04:05,225
-Wasn't that Yoon Ji-hyo just now?
-Get off. That hurts!

62
00:04:05,308 --> 00:04:07,143
What would Yoon Ji-hyo be doing here?

63
00:04:07,227 --> 00:04:09,563
Who are you? Please leave. Get out.

64
00:04:09,646 --> 00:04:10,647
He said it's not her.

65
00:04:10,730 --> 00:04:12,107
You must've seen wrong.

66
00:04:12,190 --> 00:04:13,358
-It was her.
-Get out.

67
00:04:13,441 --> 00:04:15,435
-Why would Yoon Ji-hyo be here?
-Hey, let go!

68
00:04:15,527 --> 00:04:17,696
-No, babe. It's not her.
-Get off me!

69
00:04:41,094 --> 00:04:42,470
Wake up, Shin Seo-ri.

70
00:04:43,096 --> 00:04:44,180
We're here.

71
00:04:45,223 --> 00:04:46,349
Already?

72
00:04:49,769 --> 00:04:50,770
This is not my house.

73
00:04:50,854 --> 00:04:52,147
Yeah, it's my house.

74
00:04:54,232 --> 00:04:56,776
You're not going anywhere alone today.
Resistance is futile.

75
00:05:13,001 --> 00:05:15,170
It is practically the size of a field.

76
00:05:16,963 --> 00:05:20,050
It would take three days and nights
just to roll across from here to there.

77
00:05:20,592 --> 00:05:21,968
Don't exaggerate.

78
00:05:26,306 --> 00:05:29,184
Namsan Tower looks so huge.

79
00:05:29,267 --> 00:05:31,353
Cha Se-gye,
you have really made it in the world.

80
00:05:31,436 --> 00:05:32,896
It was not all bluff.

81
00:05:35,023 --> 00:05:36,816
But you are destitute now.

82
00:05:38,276 --> 00:05:39,694
Then will this house be seized soon?

83
00:05:39,778 --> 00:05:41,404
Seized? No way.

84
00:05:41,488 --> 00:05:43,365
Who cares if you have
that view of Namsan Tower?

85
00:05:43,448 --> 00:05:45,031
When only a rocky road awaits you.

86
00:05:45,131 --> 00:05:46,576
Who knows when this will be seized?

87
00:05:46,660 --> 00:05:48,662
Might as well take it all in
while I still can.

88
00:05:50,747 --> 00:05:53,583
You're treating me
like I'm some dirt-poor pauper.

89
00:05:54,626 --> 00:05:55,543
So pretty.

90
00:05:55,627 --> 00:05:57,420
Look at it sparkle.

91
00:06:00,465 --> 00:06:02,384
I didn't mean for the invite
to be so slapdash.

92
00:06:02,467 --> 00:06:03,385
But just so you know,

93
00:06:03,468 --> 00:06:05,387
you're the first woman I've brought home.

94
00:06:05,470 --> 00:06:08,014
Think of this as your own home
and make yourself comfortable--

95
00:06:08,098 --> 00:06:09,891
I am already comfortable.
Why would I not be?

96
00:06:09,975 --> 00:06:11,184
Oh, you're already comfortable.

97
00:06:11,267 --> 00:06:12,560
Quick to adapt, as expected.

98
00:06:12,644 --> 00:06:15,355
Right, I am going to lie down
and relax for a bit.

99
00:06:21,653 --> 00:06:23,738
Maybe that's a bit too relaxed?

100
00:06:26,866 --> 00:06:28,493
It's just the two of us here.

101
00:06:38,545 --> 00:06:39,546
Hey.

102
00:06:40,755 --> 00:06:41,756
Well…

103
00:06:43,049 --> 00:06:44,217
Go lie down in the bedroom.

104
00:06:46,428 --> 00:06:48,763
The bed there is plusher
and more comfortable.

105
00:06:48,847 --> 00:06:49,931
Cha Se-gye.

106
00:06:51,141 --> 00:06:53,184
I may have followed you in
because I did not have

107
00:06:53,268 --> 00:06:54,561
the energy to argue with you,

108
00:06:54,644 --> 00:06:57,063
but my heart has yet to give you
consent to go that far.

109
00:06:58,565 --> 00:06:59,733
I see.

110
00:07:02,736 --> 00:07:05,613
Turns out the struggle continues.

111
00:07:19,085 --> 00:07:20,503
<i>Help me!</i>

112
00:07:21,004 --> 00:07:22,088
Help…

113
00:07:24,924 --> 00:07:26,468
<i>What was that?</i>

114
00:07:26,551 --> 00:07:28,511
<i>A childhood memory</i>
<i>from the master of this body?</i>

115
00:07:28,595 --> 00:07:31,639
<i>When your vital energy returns,</i>
<i>it will guide Your Highness's soul.</i>

116
00:07:32,140 --> 00:07:35,852
<i>Is this body already preparing itself</i>
<i>to welcome back its master?</i>

117
00:07:35,935 --> 00:07:38,480
<i>Could that be why dormant memories stir?</i>

118
00:07:40,065 --> 00:07:41,149
What?

119
00:07:43,068 --> 00:07:44,235
Mommy!

120
00:07:45,278 --> 00:07:47,781
-Consent or not, I don't care.
-Hey, Cha Se-gye!

121
00:07:49,115 --> 00:07:50,450
Cha Se-gye.

122
00:07:51,409 --> 00:07:52,744
Cha Se-gye!

123
00:07:53,244 --> 00:07:55,246
I'm doing this day in and day out,

124
00:07:55,330 --> 00:07:56,873
and I can't even make minimum wage.

125
00:07:56,956 --> 00:08:00,251
<i>When, oh when, will I ever</i>

126
00:08:00,335 --> 00:08:03,963
<i>Escape these streets</i>

127
00:08:04,047 --> 00:08:08,259
<i>I'm not asking for a luxury high-rise</i>

128
00:08:08,343 --> 00:08:12,514
<i>Just spare me the monthly room rental life</i>

129
00:08:23,483 --> 00:08:24,901
<i>What is your name?</i>

130
00:08:24,984 --> 00:08:26,611
My name is Dan-sim.

131
00:08:26,694 --> 00:08:27,821
Kang Dan-sim.

132
00:08:31,741 --> 00:08:33,034
Oh my.

133
00:08:33,118 --> 00:08:34,285
Goodness.

134
00:08:34,369 --> 00:08:35,662
What's this now?

135
00:08:35,745 --> 00:08:37,163
Seriously?

136
00:08:37,247 --> 00:08:39,124
Even my <i>hwagyeong</i> has been awakened now?

137
00:08:39,624 --> 00:08:41,042
Jeez.

138
00:08:54,013 --> 00:08:55,306
Stop staring.

139
00:08:55,390 --> 00:08:57,225
A demon has entered your eyes.

140
00:08:57,308 --> 00:08:58,560
Go away, demon.

141
00:08:58,643 --> 00:08:59,769
Shoo.

142
00:09:00,937 --> 00:09:03,356
Talking nonsense again.
You must be feeling better.

143
00:09:04,440 --> 00:09:06,568
Don't worry tonight and get some sleep.

144
00:09:07,902 --> 00:09:09,654
I'll take care of everything tomorrow.

145
00:09:11,072 --> 00:09:12,407
You always say that.

146
00:09:12,490 --> 00:09:14,868
Try finding a man in Korea
more capable than me.

147
00:09:14,951 --> 00:09:17,120
This isn't me talking big. This is a fact.

148
00:09:17,203 --> 00:09:19,247
If you are so capable,
how did you end up destitute?

149
00:09:21,040 --> 00:09:22,208
I'll turn that around too.

150
00:09:23,042 --> 00:09:26,087
I totally blindsided Choi Mun-do today.

151
00:09:26,588 --> 00:09:28,631
You should've seen the look on his face.

152
00:09:30,383 --> 00:09:32,302
No, scrap that. You'll ruin your eyes.

153
00:09:39,809 --> 00:09:41,519
You know, I've been feeling good recently.

154
00:09:43,396 --> 00:09:44,814
Everything hit the fan…

155
00:09:47,358 --> 00:09:48,568
but strangely, I feel good.

156
00:09:50,361 --> 00:09:52,155
Maybe it's because you're by my side?

157
00:09:54,407 --> 00:09:55,658
In hindsight…

158
00:09:57,660 --> 00:09:59,454
I think I needed something to hold on to.

159
00:09:59,996 --> 00:10:01,206
Money, honor,

160
00:10:01,789 --> 00:10:02,665
status.

161
00:10:03,791 --> 00:10:04,792
Things like that.

162
00:10:04,876 --> 00:10:07,420
I had to hold on to something
to feel like I was alive.

163
00:10:07,503 --> 00:10:09,881
Running like a car without brakes,

164
00:10:09,964 --> 00:10:12,258
it felt like I was speeding
through the void.

165
00:10:12,342 --> 00:10:15,595
But after aimlessly drifting,
going nowhere,

166
00:10:15,678 --> 00:10:18,056
and crashing hard, I finally get it.

167
00:10:18,556 --> 00:10:19,766
What's really important.

168
00:10:21,476 --> 00:10:24,062
What I truly need.

169
00:10:25,939 --> 00:10:27,023
I just…

170
00:10:30,777 --> 00:10:32,445
I just need you.

171
00:10:37,909 --> 00:10:40,411
Still, having nothing at all just isn't
a good look for a man.

172
00:10:41,079 --> 00:10:42,247
Just wait a little bit.

173
00:10:42,914 --> 00:10:45,583
Watch me make it back to the top.

174
00:10:47,794 --> 00:10:49,420
Get your hopes up, Shin Seo-ri.

175
00:10:59,514 --> 00:11:00,807
How is the Chairman doing?

176
00:11:00,890 --> 00:11:02,767
<i>He's the same. Still unconscious.</i>

177
00:11:02,850 --> 00:11:04,143
<i>No major changes in vital signs.</i>

178
00:11:04,227 --> 00:11:06,229
I'll contact you immediately
if anything changes.

179
00:11:08,523 --> 00:11:11,276
Actually, you should come right now.

180
00:11:11,359 --> 00:11:12,443
Doctor!

181
00:11:12,986 --> 00:11:14,237
Doctor!

182
00:11:18,783 --> 00:11:19,659
I see.

183
00:11:19,742 --> 00:11:20,910
PRODIGAL SON RETURNS TO CHAIL

184
00:11:23,621 --> 00:11:26,291
If the witness isn't cooperating,

185
00:11:26,374 --> 00:11:29,335
it might be better to issue
an official summons first.

186
00:11:29,419 --> 00:11:32,338
Buy us some time to replace
the head of the resort TF team.

187
00:11:32,422 --> 00:11:35,300
<i>I understand. I'll have it issued</i>
<i>and summon him this week.</i>

188
00:11:35,383 --> 00:11:36,592
All right.

189
00:11:49,814 --> 00:11:52,317
I'm told the Chairman has just woken up.

190
00:11:58,740 --> 00:12:00,241
<i>Seo-ri.</i>

191
00:12:00,325 --> 00:12:02,160
My sweet girl.

192
00:12:46,704 --> 00:12:48,164
Cha Se-gye?

193
00:12:48,247 --> 00:12:49,582
Where are you?

194
00:12:51,376 --> 00:12:52,377
Did you leave?

195
00:13:18,111 --> 00:13:19,779
MY AMAZING FAN

196
00:13:21,447 --> 00:13:22,407
You're awake?

197
00:13:24,659 --> 00:13:25,827
Let's make breakfast.

198
00:13:40,049 --> 00:13:41,884
When did you put this on me?

199
00:13:42,677 --> 00:13:43,719
Who gave you permission?

200
00:13:44,387 --> 00:13:46,639
Well? Do you like it?

201
00:13:47,432 --> 00:13:48,850
Is this some sort of leash?

202
00:13:48,933 --> 00:13:50,643
Hey, who calls that a leash?

203
00:13:50,726 --> 00:13:51,644
Just give it back then.

204
00:13:51,727 --> 00:13:53,396
Who said I did not like it?

205
00:13:56,274 --> 00:13:58,192
Why are you making such a fuss
about breakfast?

206
00:13:59,235 --> 00:14:00,278
I'm a good cook.

207
00:14:02,864 --> 00:14:05,533
My nickname when I studied abroad
was Jang-geum.

208
00:14:05,616 --> 00:14:06,868
Cha Jang-geum.

209
00:14:10,204 --> 00:14:13,249
You said you were Jang-geum,
but I do not see it at all.

210
00:14:14,542 --> 00:14:17,837
For breakfast, you need some hot soup
to warm your stomach.

211
00:14:17,920 --> 00:14:19,755
What is this? It is all dried up.

212
00:14:30,099 --> 00:14:32,143
I knew you'd say that,
so I prepared something else.

213
00:14:32,226 --> 00:14:33,811
How's that for a plot twist?

214
00:14:33,895 --> 00:14:36,856
That's soup from the best restaurant
within the Four Gates.

215
00:14:39,400 --> 00:14:40,568
Ridiculous.

216
00:14:45,740 --> 00:14:46,949
Pretty.

217
00:14:49,076 --> 00:14:50,119
It looks good on you.

218
00:14:50,828 --> 00:14:53,998
I bought this and kept waiting
for the right time to give it to you.

219
00:14:54,081 --> 00:14:55,875
Today's timing was perfect.

220
00:14:58,878 --> 00:15:00,379
When did you even buy this?

221
00:15:00,463 --> 00:15:01,881
Now I feel bad.

222
00:15:02,632 --> 00:15:05,301
I have not really done anything for you.

223
00:15:06,427 --> 00:15:08,679
Seriously? Are you looking down
on my token?

224
00:15:08,763 --> 00:15:10,765
Things have been
pretty tough for me lately.

225
00:15:10,848 --> 00:15:12,558
Little things like that give me comfort.

226
00:15:14,560 --> 00:15:16,854
I've been taking
that herbal tonic regularly too.

227
00:15:20,149 --> 00:15:23,319
Thanks to you, I'm getting both
mental and physical care.

228
00:15:23,402 --> 00:15:24,445
Come on.

229
00:15:29,617 --> 00:15:31,285
If you really feel that bad about it,

230
00:15:31,827 --> 00:15:33,621
I'll give you a chance to make up for it.

231
00:15:35,122 --> 00:15:36,666
I'll look forward to our 100th day.

232
00:15:37,291 --> 00:15:38,543
What?

233
00:15:43,714 --> 00:15:44,590
What?

234
00:15:46,425 --> 00:15:47,969
Were you not planning to celebrate it?

235
00:15:51,389 --> 00:15:53,140
That's hurtful.

236
00:15:56,185 --> 00:15:57,687
So, what should we do for our 100th?

237
00:15:58,229 --> 00:15:59,647
That was just a joke.

238
00:16:00,147 --> 00:16:01,732
Just let me know.
I'll prepare everything.

239
00:16:03,985 --> 00:16:05,069
Our 100th day?

240
00:16:05,987 --> 00:16:07,196
Well, you know…

241
00:16:08,239 --> 00:16:10,074
That sort of stuff

242
00:16:10,157 --> 00:16:11,617
used to make me cringe too.

243
00:16:11,701 --> 00:16:14,078
But I thought I'd try it out with you.

244
00:16:18,291 --> 00:16:19,375
What?

245
00:16:21,627 --> 00:16:22,795
Too cheesy?

246
00:16:23,671 --> 00:16:25,590
Is it too childish
if we're not in middle school?

247
00:16:27,633 --> 00:16:28,759
But I…

248
00:16:30,011 --> 00:16:31,679
want to try all of it with you.

249
00:16:38,019 --> 00:16:39,312
Such a fool.

250
00:16:54,785 --> 00:16:56,287
<i>I do not want to lose you.</i>

251
00:16:56,370 --> 00:16:57,955
<i>I want to keep seeing you.</i>

252
00:16:58,539 --> 00:17:00,708
<i>Could you keep smiling like that</i>

253
00:17:01,500 --> 00:17:03,252
<i>even if you knew I would disappear?</i>

254
00:17:16,140 --> 00:17:17,350
CHIEF OF STAFF SON JAE-HAN

255
00:17:19,852 --> 00:17:21,020
Give me a second.

256
00:17:33,908 --> 00:17:35,034
-When?
<i>-Yes.</i>

257
00:17:35,117 --> 00:17:37,370
<i>He woke up at dawn yesterday</i>
<i>and fell back asleep.</i>

258
00:17:37,453 --> 00:17:39,538
<i>He's undergoing</i>
<i>a thorough examination right now.</i>

259
00:17:41,290 --> 00:17:43,542
But why is the hospital
only telling us now?

260
00:17:44,168 --> 00:17:45,836
All right. Have the car ready immediately.

261
00:17:47,672 --> 00:17:50,841
<i>Even today, the ill-omened star</i>
<i>hangs in the Seoul sky.</i>

262
00:17:50,925 --> 00:17:54,011
<i>It appears this red comet,</i>
<i>which had been adorning the Seoul sky</i>

263
00:17:54,095 --> 00:17:56,931
<i>for over three months,</i>
<i>is about to set off on a long journey.</i>

264
00:17:57,014 --> 00:17:59,600
<i>In about 15 days,</i>
<i>it will leave Earth's orbit</i>

265
00:17:59,684 --> 00:18:02,603
<i>and vanish once more</i>
<i>into the unknown darkness</i>

266
00:18:02,687 --> 00:18:04,355
<i>of the far side of the universe.</i>

267
00:18:04,438 --> 00:18:06,941
<i>Vanish into the darkness…</i>

268
00:18:07,608 --> 00:18:10,277
It's a relief
that the Chairman woke up, isn't it?

269
00:18:10,778 --> 00:18:12,279
Yes, it is a relief.

270
00:18:12,363 --> 00:18:14,907
Still, it's comforting to know
that he has you by his side

271
00:18:14,993 --> 00:18:15,994
at a time like this.

272
00:18:16,094 --> 00:18:18,285
He has changed a lot, thanks to you.

273
00:18:19,787 --> 00:18:21,038
He almost seems human now.

274
00:18:21,122 --> 00:18:24,500
He may come across as prickly,
but inside he's really not like that.

275
00:18:24,583 --> 00:18:26,711
He may look thick-skinned
after all that criticism,

276
00:18:26,794 --> 00:18:28,671
but no one ever truly grows numb to that.

277
00:18:28,754 --> 00:18:30,047
He's probably just pretending.

278
00:18:30,131 --> 00:18:31,173
Right.

279
00:18:32,925 --> 00:18:34,218
Never truly numb.

280
00:18:38,222 --> 00:18:39,140
Father!

281
00:18:39,223 --> 00:18:40,558
Father!

282
00:18:40,641 --> 00:18:42,351
-Father!
-I thought you were dying.

283
00:18:42,435 --> 00:18:43,477
Do you even know

284
00:18:43,561 --> 00:18:45,062
-how devastated I was?
-Father.

285
00:18:45,688 --> 00:18:47,440
That hurts, you brat!

286
00:18:47,523 --> 00:18:50,401
Good grief. Did you forget
you're built like a mountain?

287
00:18:51,277 --> 00:18:53,529
Our father is back.
That's our father all right.

288
00:18:53,612 --> 00:18:54,822
Just look at that fiery temper.

289
00:18:54,905 --> 00:18:56,824
All his mental faculties
are as sharp as ever.

290
00:18:57,408 --> 00:18:59,034
All the test results came back clear.

291
00:18:59,660 --> 00:19:01,036
Thank goodness for that.

292
00:19:01,120 --> 00:19:03,914
Everyone was so worried
because you wouldn't wake up.

293
00:19:03,998 --> 00:19:05,291
Hey, Choi Mun-do.

294
00:19:05,374 --> 00:19:09,044
Look at you slapping on
your second face for Father.

295
00:19:09,128 --> 00:19:11,714
Father, don't believe a word
this punk Choi Mun-do says.

296
00:19:11,797 --> 00:19:13,799
If you only knew
the wicked things he did

297
00:19:13,883 --> 00:19:17,136
while you were lying in that bed…

298
00:19:17,219 --> 00:19:19,555
Are you talking
about his interim CEO appointment?

299
00:19:19,638 --> 00:19:21,182
You're already all caught up.

300
00:19:22,349 --> 00:19:24,351
You're finished now.

301
00:19:24,435 --> 00:19:27,980
Mun-do went behind our backs
and got every single executive

302
00:19:28,063 --> 00:19:29,565
in his pocket.

303
00:19:29,648 --> 00:19:31,942
How else could he have gotten that
railroaded through

304
00:19:32,026 --> 00:19:33,944
with a majority that fast?

305
00:19:34,028 --> 00:19:36,238
Now that Father is up and about,

306
00:19:36,322 --> 00:19:39,408
you better not argue and step down
from the CEO position immediately.

307
00:19:39,492 --> 00:19:40,868
Don't let things get ugly.

308
00:19:40,951 --> 00:19:43,579
Why would he? If anything,
it should get ugly for you two.

309
00:19:43,662 --> 00:19:45,623
If you two hadn't made
such a mess of things,

310
00:19:45,706 --> 00:19:48,542
maybe the board wouldn't have
skipped over my own children

311
00:19:48,626 --> 00:19:51,212
to appoint Mun-do as the interim CEO.

312
00:19:51,295 --> 00:19:53,631
You remain clueless
about your own shortcomings,

313
00:19:53,714 --> 00:19:54,965
yet you corner Mun-do!

314
00:19:55,049 --> 00:19:56,383
Father!

315
00:19:56,467 --> 00:19:58,761
You need to listen to me.
You can't trust this punk.

316
00:19:58,844 --> 00:20:00,429
This whole situation right now

317
00:20:00,513 --> 00:20:02,973
was orchestrated by Choi Mun-do.

318
00:20:03,057 --> 00:20:04,266
That's enough!

319
00:20:04,350 --> 00:20:06,560
I can't believe I must claim

320
00:20:06,644 --> 00:20:09,522
you two imbeciles as my children.

321
00:20:10,105 --> 00:20:11,357
My goodness.

322
00:20:14,193 --> 00:20:15,736
Grandfather.

323
00:20:15,820 --> 00:20:17,738
Se-gye, you're here.

324
00:20:18,239 --> 00:20:21,158
Se-gye, you should say
something to Grandfather too.

325
00:20:21,242 --> 00:20:22,785
Yeah, Se-gye.

326
00:20:22,868 --> 00:20:26,038
This is your chance to tell him in detail
about all the atrocious things

327
00:20:26,121 --> 00:20:27,289
that punk has done--

328
00:20:27,373 --> 00:20:29,750
When it comes to atrocities,
he's the worst offender.

329
00:20:29,834 --> 00:20:31,502
What? Carcinogens?

330
00:20:31,585 --> 00:20:34,129
Were you so blinded by money
that you sold your conscience?

331
00:20:34,213 --> 00:20:36,674
Even when they all called you
a money-grubber,

332
00:20:36,757 --> 00:20:37,758
I just let it go.

333
00:20:37,842 --> 00:20:40,719
After acting like you're better
than everybody else and walking out,

334
00:20:40,803 --> 00:20:43,389
this is the best you could do?
This seedy little scheme?

335
00:20:43,472 --> 00:20:47,226
Without Mun-do's investment,
you'd have fallen flat on your face, punk!

336
00:20:47,726 --> 00:20:51,146
None of you are qualified
to be CEO or President.

337
00:20:51,689 --> 00:20:53,315
Get out of my sight, the whole lot of you.

338
00:21:06,453 --> 00:21:08,873
Still, I thought blood would run
thicker than water.

339
00:21:08,956 --> 00:21:11,333
Who knew he relied
on Mun-do that much?

340
00:21:12,251 --> 00:21:13,294
Se-gye,

341
00:21:13,377 --> 00:21:15,170
why didn't you speak up in there?

342
00:21:15,254 --> 00:21:16,839
You should've said something.

343
00:21:16,922 --> 00:21:18,966
I guess he has a conscience.

344
00:21:19,049 --> 00:21:21,468
Se-gye, you should know
we were unjustly dragged down

345
00:21:21,552 --> 00:21:22,928
by your sinking ship.

346
00:21:23,012 --> 00:21:25,055
Is Grandfather really okay?

347
00:21:28,267 --> 00:21:29,852
Sensory reactions are normal again,

348
00:21:29,935 --> 00:21:31,687
and the swelling
in the brain has gone down.

349
00:21:31,770 --> 00:21:32,730
What about

350
00:21:33,272 --> 00:21:35,399
the aftereffects you mentioned?

351
00:21:35,482 --> 00:21:39,236
There's a temporary memory gap
of about two weeks before the accident.

352
00:21:39,320 --> 00:21:41,947
But he's recovering well,
so let's keep an eye on it.

353
00:21:42,031 --> 00:21:42,907
Okay.

354
00:21:42,990 --> 00:21:44,575
-Thank you.
-Sure.

355
00:21:51,290 --> 00:21:52,416
Mun-do,

356
00:21:52,499 --> 00:21:54,335
you've been through a lot.

357
00:21:55,044 --> 00:21:57,838
Thanks to you, the company survived.

358
00:21:59,256 --> 00:22:00,507
Not at all, Uncle.

359
00:22:01,842 --> 00:22:03,969
You should also make peace
with the rest of the family.

360
00:22:04,511 --> 00:22:06,430
And give Se-gye a chance
to make things right.

361
00:22:06,513 --> 00:22:08,974
He must have developed
business acumen through his startup.

362
00:22:09,058 --> 00:22:11,435
I'm sure he'll really prove
himself this time.

363
00:22:12,519 --> 00:22:13,896
Yes, sure.

364
00:22:16,148 --> 00:22:18,275
You're absolutely right.

365
00:22:24,490 --> 00:22:25,741
<i>Interim guardian?</i>

366
00:22:25,824 --> 00:22:26,742
Yes.

367
00:22:26,825 --> 00:22:29,620
Your cousin wanted us to contact
the family after daybreak.

368
00:22:29,703 --> 00:22:32,039
And he requested that family visits

369
00:22:32,122 --> 00:22:33,582
be restricted for the time being.

370
00:22:33,666 --> 00:22:35,376
-Unbelievable.
-Though mild,

371
00:22:35,459 --> 00:22:37,211
he is still suffering from aftereffects.

372
00:22:37,294 --> 00:22:39,171
Absolute rest
is the top priority right now,

373
00:22:39,254 --> 00:22:41,548
and as his attending physician,
I am of the same opinion.

374
00:22:48,305 --> 00:22:49,556
How diligent you are,

375
00:22:49,640 --> 00:22:50,933
Choi Mun-do.

376
00:22:55,938 --> 00:22:56,855
FORTUNE TELLING

377
00:22:56,939 --> 00:22:59,024
Why do you look so miserable?

378
00:22:59,108 --> 00:23:01,485
Your Highness, you see…

379
00:23:02,903 --> 00:23:04,655
Your <i>hwagyeong</i> has been awakened? Now?

380
00:23:04,738 --> 00:23:06,573
I know I may look spiritually powerful,

381
00:23:06,657 --> 00:23:08,826
like I could perform a mighty sword dance,

382
00:23:08,909 --> 00:23:10,327
but the truth is,

383
00:23:10,411 --> 00:23:12,287
I'm a sham shaman.

384
00:23:12,371 --> 00:23:14,707
No matter how much I trained
since I was young,

385
00:23:14,790 --> 00:23:16,250
my spiritual eye wouldn't open.

386
00:23:16,333 --> 00:23:17,501
The only thing

387
00:23:18,210 --> 00:23:20,170
that got sharper was my tongue.

388
00:23:20,254 --> 00:23:22,589
I never in a million years imagined

389
00:23:22,673 --> 00:23:24,675
<i>that</i> would suddenly awaken at this age.

390
00:23:26,010 --> 00:23:28,804
For one, you do not look
that spiritually powerful.

391
00:23:29,680 --> 00:23:30,848
Right.

392
00:23:31,432 --> 00:23:32,808
But if you are this faint-hearted…

393
00:23:33,434 --> 00:23:35,894
Your <i>hwagyeong</i> has been awakened,
and you have found your voice.

394
00:23:35,978 --> 00:23:37,396
You will soon be channeling spirits.

395
00:23:40,399 --> 00:23:41,817
Well, for now,

396
00:23:41,900 --> 00:23:43,694
I can only see Your Highness.

397
00:23:43,777 --> 00:23:46,238
It's tolerable for the time being.

398
00:23:46,739 --> 00:23:47,656
You can see me?

399
00:23:47,740 --> 00:23:48,949
Yes.

400
00:23:49,033 --> 00:23:51,785
You were back in Joseon.

401
00:23:51,869 --> 00:23:55,080
You said your name was Kang Dan-sim.

402
00:23:58,250 --> 00:23:59,626
Kang Dan-sim.

403
00:24:02,296 --> 00:24:04,673
I came clutching at straws.

404
00:24:06,633 --> 00:24:07,593
But I am to leave?

405
00:24:08,719 --> 00:24:11,013
So I must have seen
her childhood for a reason.

406
00:24:11,722 --> 00:24:12,848
Her childhood?

407
00:24:12,931 --> 00:24:15,184
I believe it is a childhood memory
of this body's master.

408
00:24:16,643 --> 00:24:19,313
Tangled memories.
Phantom voices out of the blue.

409
00:24:19,396 --> 00:24:20,689
That must mean…

410
00:24:22,566 --> 00:24:24,485
the body's master is on her way back?

411
00:24:24,568 --> 00:24:28,447
That would make sense
if her soul were still alive in Joseon.

412
00:24:28,530 --> 00:24:30,449
But there's no way of knowing.

413
00:24:30,532 --> 00:24:32,910
Who knows if her soul is alive or dead?

414
00:24:32,993 --> 00:24:33,911
She is alive.

415
00:24:33,994 --> 00:24:36,997
My body remains in a deathly trance
back in Joseon.

416
00:24:37,081 --> 00:24:37,998
I see.

417
00:24:38,082 --> 00:24:39,249
That body would not be alive

418
00:24:40,167 --> 00:24:42,294
if it had no soul inside it.

419
00:24:51,929 --> 00:24:53,472
<i>Yes, sure.</i>

420
00:24:53,555 --> 00:24:55,099
You're absolutely right.

421
00:25:01,730 --> 00:25:02,898
Are you insane?

422
00:25:02,981 --> 00:25:04,191
Interim guardian?

423
00:25:04,274 --> 00:25:06,485
Why? This shouldn't come as a surprise.

424
00:25:06,568 --> 00:25:10,030
Uncle trusts me above all,
even bypassing his own immediate family.

425
00:25:10,114 --> 00:25:12,032
Why the sudden fit,
like you had no idea?

426
00:25:12,116 --> 00:25:14,201
That mouth of yours has no lid.

427
00:25:14,743 --> 00:25:17,621
It's time to start minding
that tongue of yours.

428
00:25:17,704 --> 00:25:19,832
Media exposure is
only going to increase from here.

429
00:25:20,499 --> 00:25:23,001
The official Songjin Resort
meeting this week.

430
00:25:23,085 --> 00:25:24,920
Will you be attending?

431
00:25:25,003 --> 00:25:26,672
Of course.

432
00:25:26,755 --> 00:25:29,091
I'm in charge of it.
Why wouldn't I be there?

433
00:25:30,676 --> 00:25:31,677
Yeah, okay.

434
00:25:31,760 --> 00:25:33,095
I'll see you at the meeting then.

435
00:25:40,269 --> 00:25:44,898
DAEBAK BOARDING HOUSE

436
00:25:48,652 --> 00:25:50,529
<i>You were back in Joseon.</i>

437
00:25:50,612 --> 00:25:54,032
You said your name was Kang Dan-sim.

438
00:25:54,116 --> 00:25:55,909
That seals it.

439
00:25:55,993 --> 00:25:57,244
Hey, Rooftop!

440
00:25:57,327 --> 00:25:58,620
Where have you been?

441
00:25:59,288 --> 00:26:00,497
Your place right now…

442
00:26:01,412 --> 00:26:05,002
DIE

443
00:26:05,085 --> 00:26:06,170
When did this happen?

444
00:26:06,253 --> 00:26:08,755
This wasn't here yesterday.

445
00:26:08,839 --> 00:26:11,884
When I came out to shoo away
the birds that kept pooping,

446
00:26:11,967 --> 00:26:13,177
I found it like this.

447
00:26:13,260 --> 00:26:15,762
Maybe there's a curse on the building?

448
00:26:15,846 --> 00:26:18,098
First, the lightbulbs broke,

449
00:26:18,182 --> 00:26:20,350
and now there's graffiti.

450
00:26:20,434 --> 00:26:21,894
The way I see it,

451
00:26:21,977 --> 00:26:24,438
this wasn't done by one of our residents.

452
00:26:24,521 --> 00:26:26,064
It's definitely an outsider's doing.

453
00:26:26,148 --> 00:26:28,317
I should talk to the landlord about this.

454
00:26:28,400 --> 00:26:30,736
Maybe I should request
a door lock for the main entrance?

455
00:26:30,819 --> 00:26:31,945
That will never happen.

456
00:26:32,029 --> 00:26:33,071
Have I been

457
00:26:33,906 --> 00:26:35,115
under surveillance all along?

458
00:26:35,199 --> 00:26:37,326
What? Surveillance?

459
00:26:37,409 --> 00:26:38,493
By who?

460
00:26:48,652 --> 00:26:51,215
DAEBAK BOARDING HOUSE

461
00:26:58,255 --> 00:27:00,819
SPRAY PAINT

462
00:27:00,891 --> 00:27:02,976
This is truly sinister.

463
00:27:03,060 --> 00:27:05,062
What did they even use?
It's not even coming off.

464
00:27:05,145 --> 00:27:06,396
My poor back!

465
00:27:07,564 --> 00:27:09,900
I told you to leave the heavy stuff.

466
00:27:09,983 --> 00:27:11,568
Back injuries are no joke.

467
00:27:11,652 --> 00:27:13,946
We have to move this quickly
so we can sleep. I'm exhausted.

468
00:27:14,029 --> 00:27:15,530
That's why you should move tomorrow.

469
00:27:15,614 --> 00:27:17,699
Why move in the middle of the night?

470
00:27:17,783 --> 00:27:19,368
Would you be able to sleep here?

471
00:27:19,451 --> 00:27:20,786
They even wrote "Die" on the wall.

472
00:27:20,869 --> 00:27:22,955
They could easily bring
a sword to my throat at night.

473
00:27:23,038 --> 00:27:25,123
What if I get unlucky
and end up with a scar?

474
00:27:25,207 --> 00:27:26,416
I am a celebrity, after all.

475
00:27:26,500 --> 00:27:29,211
You go to extremes in everything you do.

476
00:27:29,294 --> 00:27:31,255
You overthink.
Is that why you're an actor?

477
00:27:31,338 --> 00:27:32,297
Stop.

478
00:27:32,381 --> 00:27:34,299
You better watch your mouth.

479
00:27:34,383 --> 00:27:35,968
-What?
-You better not breathe a word

480
00:27:36,051 --> 00:27:37,928
about what happened today
to Cha Se-gye.

481
00:27:38,011 --> 00:27:39,721
I do not want him worried for no reason.

482
00:27:41,515 --> 00:27:43,350
How are single people supposed to cope?

483
00:27:43,433 --> 00:27:45,185
Living in this dirty hell of couples.

484
00:27:45,269 --> 00:27:46,937
I heard Chairman Cha woke up.

485
00:27:47,646 --> 00:27:49,022
-Have you visited?
-No.

486
00:27:50,023 --> 00:27:52,609
Not yet. I had some things to sort out.

487
00:27:52,693 --> 00:27:55,028
Good. I looked into it,
and I hear Chairman Cha is dealing

488
00:27:55,112 --> 00:27:56,947
with some post-accident complications.

489
00:27:57,030 --> 00:27:58,323
Something's not right over there.

490
00:27:58,407 --> 00:27:59,700
I think it'd be best

491
00:28:00,284 --> 00:28:01,660
to wrap it all up now.

492
00:28:01,743 --> 00:28:04,162
That's not what I meant
when I said "sort out."

493
00:28:04,246 --> 00:28:05,831
Really? Then what did you mean?

494
00:28:05,914 --> 00:28:07,040
Mom, do you remember?

495
00:28:07,124 --> 00:28:09,334
Ye-jin, who tutored me
in my senior year of high school.

496
00:28:09,418 --> 00:28:12,254
She attended a top university
despite her poor background.

497
00:28:12,337 --> 00:28:14,214
You used to praise her a lot.

498
00:28:15,841 --> 00:28:18,385
I went to the department store
with a friend after finals,

499
00:28:18,468 --> 00:28:20,053
and I saw her there.

500
00:28:20,137 --> 00:28:22,931
She walked by
while affectionately holding Dad's hand.

501
00:28:23,557 --> 00:28:26,810
When I saw her the next day,
I slapped her, and then she told me

502
00:28:26,893 --> 00:28:28,103
that you knew everything.

503
00:28:28,186 --> 00:28:30,439
That you even paid her
to get lost at the right time.

504
00:28:30,522 --> 00:28:31,648
That's enough.

505
00:28:32,649 --> 00:28:34,985
Between the two of you,
I understood you even less.

506
00:28:35,068 --> 00:28:36,194
Why do you live like that?

507
00:28:36,278 --> 00:28:38,613
How are you okay
with just holding on to an empty shell?

508
00:28:43,076 --> 00:28:44,536
<i>But you know what's funny?</i>

509
00:28:44,619 --> 00:28:47,581
<i>I think I'm starting to understand</i>
<i>why you lived like a fool all these years.</i>

510
00:28:47,664 --> 00:28:49,875
<i>Why you foolishly held on</i>

511
00:28:49,958 --> 00:28:51,626
<i>and couldn't let go.</i>

512
00:28:53,378 --> 00:28:55,547
Grandfather, I'm here.

513
00:28:55,630 --> 00:28:57,424
Gosh. You're here.

514
00:28:58,884 --> 00:29:00,510
I bought some fruit.

515
00:29:01,136 --> 00:29:02,346
My goodness.

516
00:29:02,888 --> 00:29:05,307
-Did you even have time to eat today?
-No.

517
00:29:05,807 --> 00:29:06,892
I haven't yet.

518
00:29:08,018 --> 00:29:09,478
<i>I don't want to let go.</i>

519
00:29:10,020 --> 00:29:11,271
<i>It's so annoying.</i>

520
00:29:12,731 --> 00:29:15,233
It is like reaching for tears
and getting a slap on the face.

521
00:29:17,903 --> 00:29:19,738
This is actually for the better.

522
00:29:19,821 --> 00:29:21,865
It is a good chance
to sort out my next move.

523
00:29:46,014 --> 00:29:48,850
<i>In about 15 days,</i>
<i>it will leave Earth's orbit</i>

524
00:29:48,934 --> 00:29:51,728
<i>and vanish once more</i>
<i>into the unknown darkness</i>

525
00:29:51,812 --> 00:29:53,688
<i>of the far side of the universe.</i>

526
00:29:57,651 --> 00:29:58,735
Fifteen days.

527
00:30:02,489 --> 00:30:04,199
So, what should we do for our 100th day?

528
00:30:04,908 --> 00:30:06,952
Let me know
so I can prepare everything again.

529
00:30:07,035 --> 00:30:08,328
Our 100th day?

530
00:30:10,622 --> 00:30:13,375
Our 100th day will be in the spring
when flowers bloom, right?

531
00:30:13,458 --> 00:30:16,294
Then let us go see
the cornelian cherry flowers.

532
00:30:16,378 --> 00:30:18,338
We can make
some flower pancakes with the flowers.

533
00:30:18,422 --> 00:30:19,381
-Flower pancakes?
-Yeah.

534
00:30:20,048 --> 00:30:23,218
And in the summer,
we can plant trumpet vines in the yard.

535
00:30:23,301 --> 00:30:25,554
Or we can go to the sea
for the beach roses.

536
00:30:25,637 --> 00:30:28,056
Are you possessed
by a flower spirit or something?

537
00:30:28,557 --> 00:30:30,142
You want to see every flower there is.

538
00:30:31,184 --> 00:30:34,271
In the fall, we have to make
flower crowns with chrysanthemums,

539
00:30:34,354 --> 00:30:36,148
so we should plant some in the yard too.

540
00:30:36,690 --> 00:30:37,732
Right?

541
00:30:41,403 --> 00:30:42,362
Don't kid yourself.

542
00:30:49,286 --> 00:30:50,579
That's not you.

543
00:30:52,747 --> 00:30:54,124
You're just a fake.

544
00:30:56,418 --> 00:30:57,752
Get out of my body.

545
00:31:02,174 --> 00:31:04,759
<i>Seo-ri, my sweet girl.</i>

546
00:31:09,764 --> 00:31:12,309
<i>Don't kid yourself. That's not you.</i>

547
00:31:14,144 --> 00:31:15,353
I know.

548
00:31:16,521 --> 00:31:17,981
I do…

549
00:31:21,776 --> 00:31:23,278
<i>I must not dare to hope.</i>

550
00:31:30,602 --> 00:31:33,916
CHA SE-GYE

551
00:31:38,502 --> 00:31:40,754
<i>The caller you are trying</i>
<i>to reach is unavailable…</i>

552
00:31:48,637 --> 00:31:49,513
MISSED CALL
CHA SE-GYE

553
00:31:49,596 --> 00:31:51,973
<i>Call me when you see this.</i>
<i>I'll be waiting.</i>

554
00:31:56,520 --> 00:31:58,271
CHA SE-GYE: CALL ME WHEN YOU SEE THIS

555
00:32:02,817 --> 00:32:04,486
<i>If I leave without a word,</i>

556
00:32:05,070 --> 00:32:06,738
<i>you will also end up waiting for me.</i>

557
00:32:08,198 --> 00:32:10,242
YEONGHWI CHAMBER

558
00:32:14,412 --> 00:32:16,248
<i>Foolishly, just like I had,</i>

559
00:32:17,624 --> 00:32:19,292
<i>you will wait endlessly</i>

560
00:32:20,293 --> 00:32:21,670
<i>as you wither away.</i>

561
00:32:24,881 --> 00:32:27,133
<i>Word has come that the Grand Prince</i>

562
00:32:27,217 --> 00:32:29,469
<i>has breathed his last in exile.</i>

563
00:32:56,246 --> 00:32:58,290
<i>To make sure you smile</i>
<i>when you think of me,</i>

564
00:32:58,790 --> 00:33:00,875
<i>just as I picture you smiling</i>
<i>when I miss you.</i>

565
00:33:04,796 --> 00:33:06,590
<i>I shall convey this heart in full</i>

566
00:33:07,173 --> 00:33:08,758
<i>and hold nothing back.</i>

567
00:33:09,259 --> 00:33:11,011
<i>So you will not wither away alone.</i>

568
00:33:12,387 --> 00:33:13,430
<i>Right.</i>

569
00:33:14,180 --> 00:33:15,724
<i>This is not the time for tears.</i>

570
00:33:18,893 --> 00:33:22,397
CHA SE-GYE

571
00:33:22,522 --> 00:33:23,690
Hello?

572
00:33:23,773 --> 00:33:26,192
<i>Cha Se-gye, it is I, Shin Seo-ri.</i>

573
00:33:28,320 --> 00:33:30,030
Is Grandfather okay?

574
00:33:30,113 --> 00:33:31,406
He's fine, of course.

575
00:33:31,489 --> 00:33:32,991
<i>He's full of energy.</i>

576
00:33:33,074 --> 00:33:34,534
He was worried about you,

577
00:33:34,618 --> 00:33:36,536
but I told him you were perfectly fine.

578
00:33:37,871 --> 00:33:39,289
He asked that you visit soon.

579
00:33:41,249 --> 00:33:42,876
He asked for me?

580
00:33:47,464 --> 00:33:48,882
Then, before that,

581
00:33:50,300 --> 00:33:51,635
should we maybe

582
00:33:52,302 --> 00:33:53,845
go somewhere nice tomorrow?

583
00:33:53,928 --> 00:33:55,680
-Somewhere nice?
<i>-You know,</i>

584
00:33:56,306 --> 00:33:58,642
we have not been on a proper date yet.

585
00:33:58,725 --> 00:34:00,935
<i>Last time, we only went</i>
<i>where I wanted to go.</i>

586
00:34:01,019 --> 00:34:02,395
<i>So this time,</i>

587
00:34:02,479 --> 00:34:04,356
let us go where you want to go.

588
00:34:05,273 --> 00:34:06,399
I shall follow you anywhere.

589
00:34:06,483 --> 00:34:08,652
Who knows where I might take you?

590
00:34:09,986 --> 00:34:11,112
So bold.

591
00:34:11,696 --> 00:34:13,031
Anyway,

592
00:34:13,114 --> 00:34:14,616
let us go somewhere tomorrow.

593
00:34:15,116 --> 00:34:16,660
<i>Take the night to think about where.</i>

594
00:34:17,994 --> 00:34:18,870
Hello?

595
00:34:20,205 --> 00:34:21,206
Jeez.

596
00:34:21,748 --> 00:34:23,667
So aggressive.

597
00:34:24,209 --> 00:34:25,543
I was planning to steal you away.

598
00:34:29,255 --> 00:34:30,548
How could you beat me to it?

599
00:34:38,973 --> 00:34:40,225
Was I sleepwalking?

600
00:34:41,643 --> 00:34:43,478
How do you like your hair today?

601
00:34:43,561 --> 00:34:44,688
I tried extra hard today.

602
00:34:46,523 --> 00:34:47,565
Give it here.

603
00:34:50,068 --> 00:34:51,820
Charity events

604
00:34:51,903 --> 00:34:54,197
call for that wholesome look.

605
00:34:54,280 --> 00:34:55,281
Yeah.

606
00:34:56,616 --> 00:34:57,951
Like this.

607
00:35:02,455 --> 00:35:03,790
Yeah? Done.

608
00:35:04,541 --> 00:35:06,626
-You can go.
-Okay.

609
00:35:09,838 --> 00:35:12,799
So your fling with Gong Tae-woo
was really just a rumor.

610
00:35:12,882 --> 00:35:15,593
I thought Han Min-hui was fake,
and you were the real deal.

611
00:35:15,677 --> 00:35:18,638
I thought you two were secretly dating
since filming that movie.

612
00:35:19,264 --> 00:35:21,641
Are you nuts? Why would I date
a thug like Gong Tae-woo?

613
00:35:21,725 --> 00:35:24,519
And I really don't like younger guys.

614
00:35:24,602 --> 00:35:25,478
Really?

615
00:35:25,562 --> 00:35:27,772
Hey, if you don't like younger guys,

616
00:35:27,856 --> 00:35:29,107
how about a half-celebrity?

617
00:35:29,816 --> 00:35:31,109
Shin Seo-ri's manager.

618
00:35:32,068 --> 00:35:33,361
You guys looked good together.

619
00:35:34,612 --> 00:35:35,864
Are you insane?

620
00:35:35,947 --> 00:35:37,532
Half-celebrity? Please.

621
00:35:37,615 --> 00:35:40,744
Even if he has some money,
a manager is still a manager.

622
00:35:41,286 --> 00:35:43,872
-Is he well off?
-What do his parents do?

623
00:35:43,955 --> 00:35:45,582
-What neighborhood?
-Well,

624
00:35:46,166 --> 00:35:47,751
I heard they run a business or something.

625
00:35:47,834 --> 00:35:50,420
I said no.
Why would I take over that business?

626
00:35:50,503 --> 00:35:51,713
I thought this was settled.

627
00:35:53,673 --> 00:35:55,508
He always has his nose up in the air.

628
00:35:55,592 --> 00:35:57,719
He'll never be a manager
with that attitude.

629
00:35:57,802 --> 00:35:58,803
I said no.

630
00:35:58,887 --> 00:36:01,723
I will never take over
Father's department store.

631
00:36:02,348 --> 00:36:03,308
Jeez.

632
00:36:06,478 --> 00:36:07,395
"Department store"?

633
00:36:08,021 --> 00:36:09,814
But a department store in the countryside?

634
00:36:09,898 --> 00:36:12,400
It's probably just a bit bigger
than a neighborhood supermarket?

635
00:36:12,484 --> 00:36:13,735
You don't know anything.

636
00:36:13,818 --> 00:36:16,404
Department stores in the countryside
are where it's at.

637
00:36:16,488 --> 00:36:18,281
They literally rake in the money.

638
00:36:18,364 --> 00:36:20,575
Yeah, a cousin of mine

639
00:36:20,658 --> 00:36:22,410
married the son of Gumi Department Store.

640
00:36:22,494 --> 00:36:24,078
She's totally set for life now.

641
00:36:24,162 --> 00:36:26,581
She rides supercars every day,
swapping them by color.

642
00:36:26,664 --> 00:36:28,625
Shin Seo-ri, that sly fox.

643
00:36:28,708 --> 00:36:30,668
She's been sitting on that golden ticket?

644
00:36:32,670 --> 00:36:34,798
I told you no.

645
00:36:34,881 --> 00:36:37,008
I'm not doing it. I won't.

646
00:36:38,760 --> 00:36:41,888
This punk always hangs up on me.

647
00:36:41,971 --> 00:36:42,972
Ma'am, how much is this?

648
00:36:43,056 --> 00:36:44,390
Didn't you see our sign?

649
00:36:44,474 --> 00:36:46,643
Everything here is a thousand won.

650
00:36:46,726 --> 00:36:50,104
THOUSAND WON DEPARTMENT STORE

651
00:36:50,188 --> 00:36:51,940
Hey, Mr. Department Store is here.

652
00:37:11,626 --> 00:37:12,836
What are you guys doing?

653
00:37:59,424 --> 00:38:01,467
I thought you didn't like it,
but you're wearing it.

654
00:38:04,262 --> 00:38:06,306
When did I say I did not like it?

655
00:38:06,389 --> 00:38:07,557
I just called it a leash.

656
00:38:07,640 --> 00:38:10,602
But where are we going right now?

657
00:38:11,185 --> 00:38:13,146
Should I have packed an overnight bag?

658
00:38:16,482 --> 00:38:18,192
Who's the devilish one now?

659
00:38:19,235 --> 00:38:22,322
After a night at my place,
an overnight trip is nothing now?

660
00:38:23,948 --> 00:38:25,658
What are you talking about?

661
00:38:27,702 --> 00:38:29,787
We'll have to save
the overnight for next time.

662
00:38:29,871 --> 00:38:31,623
Just think of today as meeting the family.

663
00:38:32,665 --> 00:38:33,541
Meeting the family?

664
00:38:33,625 --> 00:38:35,043
We're on our way to see my mom.

665
00:38:37,879 --> 00:38:41,257
REST IN PEACE, HAN HYE-SEON

666
00:38:45,345 --> 00:38:46,471
Well?

667
00:38:47,639 --> 00:38:49,766
-Isn't my mom beautiful?
-Yeah.

668
00:38:51,184 --> 00:38:53,728
Incredibly beautiful and elegant.

669
00:38:53,811 --> 00:38:56,272
I never understood why guys
wanted their families

670
00:38:56,356 --> 00:38:58,066
to meet their girlfriends,

671
00:38:58,149 --> 00:38:59,859
but now I do.

672
00:39:00,485 --> 00:39:02,028
I wanted to show you off.

673
00:39:02,820 --> 00:39:04,364
My pretty girlfriend.

674
00:39:05,490 --> 00:39:06,908
You should have told me beforehand.

675
00:39:07,784 --> 00:39:09,202
I would have dressed up nicer.

676
00:39:09,285 --> 00:39:10,662
You're perfect.

677
00:39:10,745 --> 00:39:12,163
How much nicer could you look?

678
00:39:12,246 --> 00:39:13,957
Are you trying to show my mom up?

679
00:39:14,499 --> 00:39:16,292
Mom has something to say. Hold on.

680
00:39:19,963 --> 00:39:21,089
She says she's prettier.

681
00:39:21,631 --> 00:39:22,882
She says not to worry.

682
00:39:37,355 --> 00:39:39,774
This is the last place I came
with Mom when I was little.

683
00:39:39,857 --> 00:39:41,859
Looking at it now, it's so tiny.

684
00:39:43,027 --> 00:39:44,737
Why did you never come back as an adult?

685
00:39:45,655 --> 00:39:46,948
Worried you might think of her?

686
00:39:50,702 --> 00:39:51,703
No.

687
00:39:54,372 --> 00:39:55,540
I was afraid I'd get weak.

688
00:39:57,041 --> 00:39:59,377
Thinking of Mom just makes me
feel some kind of way.

689
00:40:01,170 --> 00:40:02,547
It brings me down sometimes.

690
00:40:04,132 --> 00:40:05,842
Mom was pretty sick when I was young.

691
00:40:06,509 --> 00:40:08,511
But she lied to me.

692
00:40:09,303 --> 00:40:10,596
She said she'd get healthy

693
00:40:10,680 --> 00:40:12,306
and come back for me.

694
00:40:13,975 --> 00:40:15,018
She told me to wait.

695
00:40:26,279 --> 00:40:27,155
Se-gye.

696
00:40:29,490 --> 00:40:30,408
Cha Se-gye.

697
00:40:34,328 --> 00:40:35,329
Come here, Se-gye.

698
00:40:44,255 --> 00:40:45,590
My dear Se-gye.

699
00:40:45,673 --> 00:40:47,091
Just wait a little bit.

700
00:40:50,803 --> 00:40:52,388
I'll come back for you.

701
00:40:52,930 --> 00:40:56,559
<i>I only realized much later</i>
<i>that she couldn't come for me.</i>

702
00:40:57,685 --> 00:40:59,312
<i>But I didn't know that at the time.</i>

703
00:40:59,395 --> 00:41:02,273
I just sat by that window,
waiting for her every day.

704
00:41:02,356 --> 00:41:03,441
Before waiting some more.

705
00:41:08,362 --> 00:41:10,448
Would it have been better
if I'd known the truth?

706
00:41:15,244 --> 00:41:16,954
I don't even know anymore.

707
00:41:19,165 --> 00:41:20,833
I think knowing the truth is better.

708
00:41:23,127 --> 00:41:25,505
-What?
-Because waiting without knowing the end…

709
00:41:27,840 --> 00:41:28,925
is just too hard.

710
00:41:35,640 --> 00:41:36,933
Cha Se-gye.

711
00:41:40,144 --> 00:41:42,647
I do not want to lie to you.

712
00:41:42,730 --> 00:41:45,066
I do not want to make you wait endlessly.

713
00:41:45,733 --> 00:41:47,527
That is why I am telling you this.

714
00:41:49,654 --> 00:41:50,947
I am going back.

715
00:41:52,865 --> 00:41:54,117
Going back?

716
00:41:58,287 --> 00:41:59,622
I have to go back

717
00:42:00,498 --> 00:42:01,707
to where I came from.

718
00:42:09,173 --> 00:42:12,468
So let us do everything we can,
starting today.

719
00:42:12,552 --> 00:42:15,012
One by one, so we do not have regrets.

720
00:42:18,808 --> 00:42:19,976
What is this?

721
00:42:20,059 --> 00:42:21,394
Are you making fun of me?

722
00:42:22,061 --> 00:42:23,437
I believed all this nonsense

723
00:42:23,521 --> 00:42:25,940
about reincarnation
and transcending time and space,

724
00:42:26,607 --> 00:42:27,733
and now you're leaving?

725
00:42:28,609 --> 00:42:30,027
You're just going to leave?

726
00:42:32,697 --> 00:42:33,698
Cha Se-gye.

727
00:42:33,781 --> 00:42:36,075
At least try to make some sense.

728
00:42:36,159 --> 00:42:38,828
If you're leaving, when are you going?
In a month? Two months?

729
00:42:40,454 --> 00:42:42,290
-That is--
-Why? Is there no deadline?

730
00:42:42,373 --> 00:42:43,875
Haven't you set a date?

731
00:42:44,625 --> 00:42:46,544
I am not sure either.

732
00:42:47,253 --> 00:42:49,088
Probably around two weeks.

733
00:42:51,507 --> 00:42:53,759
-I guess there is one.
-I know this is hard for you.

734
00:42:54,302 --> 00:42:55,553
I know it very well.

735
00:42:56,053 --> 00:42:58,973
That is why I'm not hiding it
and telling you the truth for your sake.

736
00:42:59,056 --> 00:43:00,391
For my sake?

737
00:43:00,474 --> 00:43:03,436
So you asked me out on a date today
to tell me that nonsense?

738
00:43:04,187 --> 00:43:05,188
You…

739
00:43:06,689 --> 00:43:07,815
Do you think…

740
00:43:09,817 --> 00:43:11,485
it is easy for me to tell you this?

741
00:43:13,321 --> 00:43:15,781
Then what do you want? Applause?

742
00:43:15,865 --> 00:43:18,284
Should I get you a palanquin
so you can return in glory?

743
00:43:18,367 --> 00:43:20,745
What did you possibly expect from me

744
00:43:20,828 --> 00:43:22,830
when you came to me with such nonsense?

745
00:43:24,415 --> 00:43:26,042
-You…
-Why mess with me like this

746
00:43:26,125 --> 00:43:28,044
if you were just going to leave anyway?

747
00:43:28,127 --> 00:43:30,838
You turned someone barely holding it
together into a lovesick moron.

748
00:43:30,922 --> 00:43:32,048
Right now, I…

749
00:43:32,131 --> 00:43:33,257
No, you can't go.

750
00:43:34,175 --> 00:43:35,509
I refuse, so just know that.

751
00:43:35,593 --> 00:43:36,719
Cha Se-gye.

752
00:43:37,887 --> 00:43:38,763
No.

753
00:43:39,972 --> 00:43:42,808
I'm the crazy one for believing
everything you said until now.

754
00:43:44,227 --> 00:43:45,728
We're going to see a doctor tomorrow.

755
00:43:45,811 --> 00:43:47,605
We'll get an EEG or whatever.

756
00:43:47,688 --> 00:43:50,191
Just get a full checkup,
and then we can talk.

757
00:43:50,858 --> 00:43:51,943
This is just…

758
00:43:53,736 --> 00:43:54,946
Damn it.

759
00:44:09,710 --> 00:44:11,587
I do not want to leave either.

760
00:44:13,756 --> 00:44:15,967
I want to stay by your side.

761
00:45:10,977 --> 00:45:13,441
MY AMAZING FAN

762
00:45:25,953 --> 00:45:28,080
<i>If only I could take it with me.</i>

763
00:45:28,164 --> 00:45:31,125
<i>Then I would have something to look at</i>

764
00:45:31,208 --> 00:45:33,210
<i>from time to time.</i>

765
00:45:55,149 --> 00:45:58,444
From now on, I want all the money
coming to me to be deposited here.

766
00:45:58,527 --> 00:45:59,612
Please.

767
00:46:04,450 --> 00:46:06,243
NAM OK-SUN
SONGJIN GENERAL HOSPITAL

768
00:46:07,161 --> 00:46:08,537
Are you going somewhere?

769
00:46:08,621 --> 00:46:11,999
Now that the drama is over,
are you going on a trip or something?

770
00:46:13,042 --> 00:46:14,001
A trip?

771
00:46:14,085 --> 00:46:15,628
Actually, I'm glad you're here today.

772
00:46:16,170 --> 00:46:19,048
You should have this picture.

773
00:46:19,131 --> 00:46:20,257
Picture?

774
00:46:21,509 --> 00:46:23,260
I found it while cleaning the storage.

775
00:46:35,189 --> 00:46:36,857
I'll pay you back soon.

776
00:46:36,941 --> 00:46:38,901
Seo-ri, my dearest daughter.

777
00:46:38,984 --> 00:46:40,444
When you wake up from your nap,

778
00:46:41,362 --> 00:46:42,446
we should be home.

779
00:46:44,824 --> 00:46:46,325
I was right.

780
00:46:47,868 --> 00:46:49,453
That was a childhood memory.

781
00:46:49,537 --> 00:46:50,746
Do you remember?

782
00:46:55,960 --> 00:46:57,211
She will be back soon.

783
00:46:58,504 --> 00:47:00,047
<i>Once I am gone.</i>

784
00:47:03,342 --> 00:47:05,428
<i>My name is Dan-sim.</i>

785
00:47:05,511 --> 00:47:07,096
<i>Kang Dan-sim.</i>

786
00:47:07,179 --> 00:47:09,181
That tone…

787
00:47:13,936 --> 00:47:15,980
What is your name?

788
00:47:16,063 --> 00:47:17,898
My name is Dan-sim.

789
00:47:17,982 --> 00:47:18,941
Kang Dan-sim.

790
00:47:21,861 --> 00:47:24,488
Just as I thought. Her tone…

791
00:47:26,073 --> 00:47:27,741
I don't think it's Her Highness.

792
00:47:30,494 --> 00:47:32,413
Maybe she's not going back?

793
00:47:32,496 --> 00:47:33,539
<i>Here is our next story.</i>

794
00:47:33,622 --> 00:47:36,584
<i>According to the BBC,</i>
<i>five Joseon-era artifacts</i>

795
00:47:36,667 --> 00:47:40,129
<i>currently held at the British Museum</i>
<i>are set to be repatriated.</i>

796
00:47:40,212 --> 00:47:43,132
<i>Among the items to be returned</i>
<i>is reportedly a diary belonging</i>

797
00:47:43,215 --> 00:47:46,177
<i>to Grand Prince Cheongheon,</i>
<i>the younger brother of Anjong of Joseon,</i>

798
00:47:46,260 --> 00:47:49,180
<i>who is also known</i>
<i>as the "ill-fated prince."</i>

799
00:47:49,805 --> 00:47:51,432
<i>The diary is currently…</i>

800
00:47:51,515 --> 00:47:53,832
How does it feel to be heading
into the heart of the enemy?

801
00:47:53,934 --> 00:47:56,645
<i>-…a painting of a court lady…</i>
-For a formal meeting and not an ambush.

802
00:47:56,729 --> 00:47:57,980
No reason to fuss.

803
00:47:58,063 --> 00:47:59,773
When did feelings get in the way of work?

804
00:47:59,857 --> 00:48:02,610
<i>…lending weight</i>
<i>to the academic hypothesis.</i>

805
00:48:06,447 --> 00:48:07,490
Step on it.

806
00:48:08,449 --> 00:48:10,701
Choi Mun-do must be
waiting anxiously for us.

807
00:48:11,494 --> 00:48:13,579
<i>I would like to thank</i>
<i>all the executives for attending</i>

808
00:48:13,662 --> 00:48:15,748
<i>the first official meeting</i>
<i>for Songjin Resort today.</i>

809
00:48:15,831 --> 00:48:18,358
The fact that you took time
out of your busy schedules

810
00:48:18,458 --> 00:48:21,712
shows that you support this project
and believe this will bring forth

811
00:48:21,795 --> 00:48:24,089
a new era for Chail.
I appreciate it greatly.

812
00:48:25,883 --> 00:48:27,968
Now, shall we begin the meeting?

813
00:48:34,391 --> 00:48:36,268
Wow…

814
00:48:36,352 --> 00:48:38,354
They're ostracizing me now.

815
00:48:38,437 --> 00:48:40,773
Ms. Nam Ok-sun's bills are fully paid.

816
00:48:40,856 --> 00:48:43,692
She's registered for automatic payments
under Mr. Cha Se-gye.

817
00:48:43,776 --> 00:48:45,778
We actually needed
her guardian's consent anyway.

818
00:48:45,861 --> 00:48:47,530
You can do it now.

819
00:48:52,243 --> 00:48:53,369
Then this too.

820
00:48:54,161 --> 00:48:55,579
Have this account be linked as well.

821
00:48:55,663 --> 00:48:59,291
So she can be well taken care of
even if you cannot reach me.

822
00:48:59,375 --> 00:49:00,960
Please.

823
00:49:08,050 --> 00:49:11,262
<i>She's registered for automatic payments</i>
<i>under Mr. Cha Se-gye.</i>

824
00:49:13,055 --> 00:49:15,683
Why mess with me like this
if you were just going to leave anyway?

825
00:49:16,475 --> 00:49:19,061
You turned someone barely holding it
together into a lovesick moron.

826
00:49:19,144 --> 00:49:20,396
<i>Right now, I…</i>

827
00:49:21,021 --> 00:49:22,147
You jerk.

828
00:49:22,982 --> 00:49:24,233
How could you say that?

829
00:49:26,277 --> 00:49:29,572
Then again, I am the worst one of all.

830
00:49:30,864 --> 00:49:32,533
Saying goodbye with a smile…

831
00:49:34,451 --> 00:49:36,036
I am one greedy wench.

832
00:50:03,105 --> 00:50:04,231
She is not in her room.

833
00:50:04,315 --> 00:50:05,482
The patient is missing!

834
00:50:05,566 --> 00:50:07,026
No need to panic.

835
00:50:07,109 --> 00:50:10,321
She didn't disappear. She just went
for a short walk right out front.

836
00:50:11,947 --> 00:50:14,742
Ma'am, do you have a moment?

837
00:50:14,825 --> 00:50:16,910
You should speak to her doctor.

838
00:50:30,966 --> 00:50:32,635
Why are you out in the cold?

839
00:50:33,344 --> 00:50:34,470
What if you catch a cold?

840
00:50:34,553 --> 00:50:37,514
It's fun sitting here like this.

841
00:50:38,223 --> 00:50:42,353
Watching people get on and off the bus
keeps me from getting bored.

842
00:50:43,062 --> 00:50:44,188
Why?

843
00:50:45,272 --> 00:50:47,274
Do you like seeing people out and about?

844
00:50:49,526 --> 00:50:50,694
No, it's not that.

845
00:50:51,820 --> 00:50:53,405
Actually…

846
00:50:55,240 --> 00:50:58,661
my dream when I was a kid
was to be a driver.

847
00:51:00,704 --> 00:51:03,707
Other kids wanted to be the bus guides.

848
00:51:03,791 --> 00:51:06,710
But I really wanted to be the driver.

849
00:51:07,795 --> 00:51:10,964
Gosh. Driving all day in a car,

850
00:51:11,507 --> 00:51:13,384
having a blast,

851
00:51:13,467 --> 00:51:16,637
making money, and seeing the world
to my heart's content.

852
00:51:16,720 --> 00:51:18,555
Living life on your own terms is enviable.

853
00:51:19,181 --> 00:51:21,558
I was so envious of that.

854
00:51:21,642 --> 00:51:23,268
A little disappointed I couldn't.

855
00:51:26,814 --> 00:51:28,732
Now, the next item on the agenda

856
00:51:28,816 --> 00:51:30,818
is the most important issue.

857
00:51:34,405 --> 00:51:35,489
Securing the site.

858
00:51:35,572 --> 00:51:37,449
Earlier at the groundbreaking ceremony,

859
00:51:37,533 --> 00:51:39,868
press releases went out saying
the site was fully secured,

860
00:51:39,952 --> 00:51:42,705
but the plot near the resort entrance
hasn't been purchased yet.

861
00:51:42,788 --> 00:51:46,083
The site purchase needs to be completed
before construction begins,

862
00:51:46,166 --> 00:51:48,210
but the owner of this plot
is very stubborn.

863
00:51:48,293 --> 00:51:49,753
You don't worry about that.

864
00:51:50,546 --> 00:51:52,923
The head of our new TF team
will take care of it.

865
00:51:53,465 --> 00:51:55,008
Isn't that right, Mr. Cha?

866
00:51:59,221 --> 00:52:00,597
What?

867
00:52:00,681 --> 00:52:03,934
I guess it hasn't been shared
with the executives yet.

868
00:52:04,017 --> 00:52:05,811
Thanks to Mr. Cha Se-gye's connections,

869
00:52:05,894 --> 00:52:08,689
we have successfully signed
a contract with the restaurant owner.

870
00:52:13,360 --> 00:52:14,570
SEORI'S NOODLE SHOP

871
00:52:14,653 --> 00:52:16,905
Thanks to the legwork he put in,

872
00:52:16,989 --> 00:52:19,533
we have finally secured 100% of the site.

873
00:52:20,284 --> 00:52:21,744
Please give him a round of applause.

874
00:52:38,635 --> 00:52:39,928
That's a good age.

875
00:52:41,388 --> 00:52:42,890
But they don't know that.

876
00:52:43,807 --> 00:52:46,596
-I'll have <i>tteokbokki.</i>
-Let's add one serving of beef brisket.

877
00:52:46,685 --> 00:52:49,938
I thought I'd be
young like that forever too.

878
00:52:50,022 --> 00:52:53,484
But I blinked, and I became an old lady.

879
00:52:54,109 --> 00:52:56,111
I was so busy rolling all that dough.

880
00:52:56,987 --> 00:52:58,697
I didn't know my hair had gone gray.

881
00:53:02,159 --> 00:53:04,203
But still,

882
00:53:04,286 --> 00:53:06,705
that doesn't mean
I didn't like running the restaurant.

883
00:53:06,789 --> 00:53:09,583
Watching kids enjoy my noodles

884
00:53:09,666 --> 00:53:11,043
made me full too.

885
00:53:11,543 --> 00:53:14,004
That's why I didn't stop working.

886
00:53:16,590 --> 00:53:17,549
But now,

887
00:53:18,342 --> 00:53:19,885
that's all over too.

888
00:53:21,845 --> 00:53:23,972
I should slowly start wrapping things up.

889
00:53:25,849 --> 00:53:28,101
Is it because
of the restaurant demolition?

890
00:53:28,602 --> 00:53:30,103
I will try to take care of that--

891
00:53:30,187 --> 00:53:31,814
No, look at me.

892
00:53:31,897 --> 00:53:33,273
How do I look to you?

893
00:53:34,107 --> 00:53:35,776
Do you think I can run a restaurant again?

894
00:53:37,361 --> 00:53:40,447
<i>Ms. Nam Ok-sun is not doing well.</i>

895
00:53:40,531 --> 00:53:42,199
While we couldn't reach you,

896
00:53:42,282 --> 00:53:44,451
her cognitive function
has dropped rapidly.

897
00:53:44,535 --> 00:53:46,340
As well as her physical function.

898
00:53:46,411 --> 00:53:48,789
You should probably prepare yourself…

899
00:53:49,790 --> 00:53:50,791
Prepare myself?

900
00:53:51,416 --> 00:53:53,627
<i>She doesn't have much time left.</i>

901
00:53:55,045 --> 00:53:57,798
Of course you can. Why not?

902
00:53:59,258 --> 00:54:00,342
No.

903
00:54:00,926 --> 00:54:03,011
I only held on to it all this time

904
00:54:03,095 --> 00:54:05,264
out of greed and sentiment.

905
00:54:09,518 --> 00:54:10,894
It's okay.

906
00:54:11,603 --> 00:54:12,855
Don't worry about it.

907
00:54:14,439 --> 00:54:16,650
Hey, it's cold out today.

908
00:54:17,359 --> 00:54:20,320
Why are you wearing such thin clothes?

909
00:54:22,364 --> 00:54:24,908
Your hands are so cold. Jeez.

910
00:54:25,659 --> 00:54:26,702
My granddaughter

911
00:54:27,911 --> 00:54:30,163
always goes around with her hands
freezing like this too.

912
00:54:30,831 --> 00:54:32,374
In a little bit,

913
00:54:32,875 --> 00:54:33,834
the sun will set.

914
00:54:34,793 --> 00:54:36,253
She's late.

915
00:54:54,313 --> 00:54:55,939
Miss, you must be cold.

916
00:54:56,023 --> 00:54:59,776
Here. Put this on, at least. Go on.

917
00:55:01,445 --> 00:55:02,654
Here you go.

918
00:55:02,738 --> 00:55:05,616
I'll lend it to you until my bus comes.

919
00:55:06,575 --> 00:55:08,660
My granddaughter bought this for me.

920
00:55:09,369 --> 00:55:10,495
How is it?

921
00:55:10,579 --> 00:55:15,167
Doesn't it feel a bit better wrapped up
all warm and cozy like this?

922
00:55:16,126 --> 00:55:17,461
It's pretty.

923
00:55:18,921 --> 00:55:20,297
No, I am…

924
00:55:23,759 --> 00:55:25,218
I am not…

925
00:55:28,180 --> 00:55:29,514
Miss, why are you crying?

926
00:55:29,598 --> 00:55:32,184
Are you upset about something?

927
00:55:34,353 --> 00:55:38,565
Oh my. You'll lose your energy
if you cry like this.

928
00:55:38,649 --> 00:55:40,901
Please don't cry.

929
00:55:48,575 --> 00:55:50,327
What's wrong with me?

930
00:55:53,747 --> 00:55:57,042
Why does my chest hurt so much?

931
00:56:01,004 --> 00:56:03,340
Don't cry, okay?

932
00:56:05,425 --> 00:56:08,095
Don't cry…

933
00:56:22,526 --> 00:56:23,860
It hurts.

934
00:56:23,944 --> 00:56:26,738
Don't cry…

935
00:56:28,949 --> 00:56:30,325
Don't cry.

936
00:56:32,369 --> 00:56:34,496
Don't cry.

937
00:56:36,498 --> 00:56:38,542
Don't cry.

938
00:56:42,462 --> 00:56:44,339
You can't go in right now…

939
00:56:55,976 --> 00:56:57,227
So this is what you wanted?

940
00:56:57,310 --> 00:56:59,438
You just wanted me to walk out on my own?

941
00:57:00,147 --> 00:57:02,024
No, why would you leave?

942
00:57:02,107 --> 00:57:03,859
I already told the Chairman

943
00:57:03,942 --> 00:57:07,070
to watch closely as you prove yourself
with the chance you were given.

944
00:57:07,154 --> 00:57:08,280
To see

945
00:57:08,905 --> 00:57:10,407
what our Crown Prince chooses.

946
00:57:10,490 --> 00:57:11,616
What?

947
00:57:11,700 --> 00:57:13,118
I guess you don't know this yet,

948
00:57:13,201 --> 00:57:15,495
but I'm more compassionate than I look.

949
00:57:15,579 --> 00:57:16,705
Look at me right now.

950
00:57:16,788 --> 00:57:19,458
I'm giving you a chance
to regain Uncle's trust.

951
00:57:19,541 --> 00:57:21,043
And also a chance

952
00:57:21,877 --> 00:57:23,420
to win love.

953
00:57:23,503 --> 00:57:25,130
Whatever you do, you'll gain something.

954
00:57:25,213 --> 00:57:27,544
Is there a reason to be this mad at me?

955
00:57:28,467 --> 00:57:30,177
Look at you having a blast.

956
00:57:30,260 --> 00:57:32,179
Your eyes light up
when you play with people.

957
00:57:32,262 --> 00:57:34,014
Yeah, I'll admit it.

958
00:57:34,639 --> 00:57:35,974
It is fun.

959
00:57:40,187 --> 00:57:42,647
But you should probably hurry up now.

960
00:57:45,192 --> 00:57:47,027
If you decide to choose her,

961
00:57:47,527 --> 00:57:48,695
you don't have much time left.

962
00:57:48,779 --> 00:57:49,738
What time?

963
00:57:49,821 --> 00:57:52,491
The demolition team should be heading
to the site right now.

964
00:57:53,408 --> 00:57:55,118
They'll arrive before sunset.

965
00:57:59,456 --> 00:58:02,584
<i>I told them to demolish</i>
<i>the entrance plot first.</i>

966
00:58:02,667 --> 00:58:06,213
To wipe out
that messy commercial area first.

967
00:58:07,464 --> 00:58:08,548
Well?

968
00:58:08,632 --> 00:58:10,258
Shouldn't you go and check on her?

969
00:58:10,342 --> 00:58:11,760
You bastard.

970
00:58:15,597 --> 00:58:17,224
There we go.

971
00:58:17,307 --> 00:58:18,725
This is the Cha Se-gye I know.

972
00:58:18,809 --> 00:58:22,354
Throwing punches without thinking
and cursing up a storm.

973
00:58:22,437 --> 00:58:24,356
Only knowing how to throw a tantrum.

974
00:58:24,439 --> 00:58:25,690
You really

975
00:58:26,650 --> 00:58:29,277
have never wanted for anything.

976
00:58:29,861 --> 00:58:32,864
Just a kid running wild
without knowing how the world works.

977
00:58:54,302 --> 00:58:55,554
Fine.

978
00:58:57,806 --> 00:58:58,849
Do whatever you want.

979
00:59:01,143 --> 00:59:04,354
Do whatever you want with the company.
Tear it apart or destroy it.

980
00:59:04,437 --> 00:59:07,691
But that messy restaurant spot
isn't important at all.

981
00:59:08,984 --> 00:59:10,861
You can easily just leave it alone.

982
00:59:12,696 --> 00:59:15,240
I haven't done a single thing right
for that woman.

983
00:59:15,323 --> 00:59:17,200
So just leave that alone.

984
00:59:19,327 --> 00:59:20,370
Is that an order?

985
00:59:21,705 --> 00:59:22,956
Or a favor?

986
00:59:24,374 --> 00:59:25,584
Pick one.

987
00:59:30,547 --> 00:59:32,090
If you step on me, I'll let you.

988
00:59:32,591 --> 00:59:34,092
If you tell me to bow, I will.

989
00:59:34,176 --> 00:59:35,594
So just let that one thing go.

990
00:59:36,303 --> 00:59:38,513
To us, it may be a messy,
insignificant restaurant,

991
00:59:38,597 --> 00:59:41,308
but for someone else,
it's their home and their life.

992
00:59:43,393 --> 00:59:44,477
So just spare them that.

993
00:59:46,479 --> 00:59:47,898
I'm begging you.

994
00:59:56,114 --> 00:59:58,408
I thought you were a kid,
but you're a man.

995
01:00:00,035 --> 01:00:02,287
Now we can finally talk.

996
01:00:02,370 --> 01:00:03,622
Right?

997
01:00:05,457 --> 01:00:06,917
But you know what, Se-gye?

998
01:00:08,126 --> 01:00:10,754
I gave the demolition team
special instructions.

999
01:00:12,172 --> 01:00:14,466
No matter who, no matter when…

1000
01:00:15,008 --> 01:00:16,551
No matter what happens,

1001
01:00:17,260 --> 01:00:19,387
they are to proceed.

1002
01:00:21,431 --> 01:00:22,724
Too bad.

1003
01:00:26,269 --> 01:00:27,312
Damn it.

1004
01:00:30,774 --> 01:00:32,609
Damn child.

1005
01:00:43,453 --> 01:00:44,371
Director Jang.

1006
01:00:46,957 --> 01:00:48,250
Please follow me.

1007
01:01:06,268 --> 01:01:07,310
Director Jang.

1008
01:01:14,776 --> 01:01:16,361
Jang Seok-ho!

1009
01:01:18,947 --> 01:01:20,115
Your Highness!

1010
01:01:21,408 --> 01:01:22,951
-Excuse me.
-Where did she go?

1011
01:01:25,203 --> 01:01:27,330
-What are you doing there?
-Her Highness.

1012
01:01:27,414 --> 01:01:30,041
No, I mean. Where did Seo-ri go?

1013
01:01:30,125 --> 01:01:31,793
She went to see her grandmother. Why?

1014
01:01:32,502 --> 01:01:34,087
I need to tell her this.

1015
01:01:34,170 --> 01:01:36,381
I need to let her know
as soon as possible.

1016
01:01:36,464 --> 01:01:38,633
Why isn't she picking up her damn phone?

1017
01:01:38,717 --> 01:01:41,177
What are you talking about?
You can tell me.

1018
01:01:42,095 --> 01:01:43,013
No. It's--

1019
01:01:43,096 --> 01:01:44,931
I'm her manager.

1020
01:01:46,683 --> 01:01:47,892
Just tell me.

1021
01:01:48,585 --> 01:01:51,099
SEORI'S NOODLE SHOP

1022
01:02:00,572 --> 01:02:01,893
2025 TO 2026

1023
01:02:20,884 --> 01:02:22,344
So meticulous.

1024
01:02:27,557 --> 01:02:29,309
<i>You know, I've been feeling good recently.</i>

1025
01:02:29,392 --> 01:02:32,187
<i>Everything hit the fan,</i>
<i>but strangely, I feel good.</i>

1026
01:02:32,270 --> 01:02:33,563
<i>You idiot.</i>

1027
01:02:33,646 --> 01:02:35,357
I think I needed something to hold on to.

1028
01:02:35,440 --> 01:02:37,859
I had to hold on to something
to feel like I was alive.

1029
01:02:39,069 --> 01:02:41,112
<i>All caught up in your own damn feelings.</i>

1030
01:02:41,613 --> 01:02:42,614
I finally get it.

1031
01:02:43,281 --> 01:02:44,491
What's really important.

1032
01:02:44,991 --> 01:02:48,203
What I truly need.

1033
01:02:49,454 --> 01:02:51,956
<i>You don't know anything.</i>

1034
01:02:52,665 --> 01:02:53,750
I just…

1035
01:02:54,793 --> 01:02:56,378
I just need you.

1036
01:02:58,088 --> 01:03:01,174
<i>I was completely oblivious to the despair</i>

1037
01:03:02,467 --> 01:03:04,010
<i>you've shouldered alone.</i>

1038
01:03:08,640 --> 01:03:10,850
<i>It's not cabbage. It's basically gold now.</i>

1039
01:03:10,934 --> 01:03:13,978
<i>It's so ridiculous.</i>
<i>I might just start farming it myself.</i>

1040
01:03:15,522 --> 01:03:17,607
<i>The sign across the street says</i>
<i>they're the original.</i>

1041
01:03:17,690 --> 01:03:20,902
<i>The original </i>kalguksu?
<i>They're making me laugh nonstop.</i>

1042
01:03:21,945 --> 01:03:23,613
Half of this is just swearing.

1043
01:03:25,156 --> 01:03:26,783
Such a foul mouth she has.

1044
01:03:28,618 --> 01:03:29,828
<i>Oh my, that little brat.</i>

1045
01:03:29,911 --> 01:03:32,705
<i>When I told her to eat some carrots,</i>
<i>she threw a fit and pinched me.</i>

1046
01:03:32,789 --> 01:03:34,499
<i>For a little thing,</i>
<i>she's got a strong grip.</i>

1047
01:03:44,634 --> 01:03:46,261
Grandma, I'm home.

1048
01:03:46,344 --> 01:03:48,763
My sweet girl. You're home.

1049
01:03:49,472 --> 01:03:50,723
-Let's eat some carrots!
-What?

1050
01:03:50,807 --> 01:03:52,308
-Let's eat some carrots!
-I said no!

1051
01:03:52,392 --> 01:03:53,601
-I don't want to!
-Come on!

1052
01:03:53,685 --> 01:03:54,602
I hate carrots.

1053
01:03:54,686 --> 01:03:57,439
That hurts! You little brat.

1054
01:03:57,522 --> 01:03:58,731
My goodness.

1055
01:04:08,241 --> 01:04:11,327
<i>My Seo-ri is on TV.</i>

1056
01:04:11,870 --> 01:04:14,330
<i>I was so excited that I gave</i>
<i>everything away for free today.</i>

1057
01:04:14,414 --> 01:04:16,082
Look at my sweet girl.

1058
01:04:16,166 --> 01:04:19,961
<i>I'm so glad Dong-seok took her to Seoul.</i>

1059
01:04:20,044 --> 01:04:22,046
<i>He should have taken her sooner.</i>

1060
01:04:23,381 --> 01:04:26,134
<i>My Seo-ri is on every time</i>
<i>I turn on the TV.</i>

1061
01:04:26,718 --> 01:04:28,845
<i>I mean, I'm happy about it,</i>

1062
01:04:29,971 --> 01:04:32,849
<i>but is she doing okay in school?</i>

1063
01:04:32,932 --> 01:04:34,058
<i>Is she eating well?</i>

1064
01:04:34,601 --> 01:04:37,145
<i>I'm worried because</i>
<i>she's as skinny as a skewer.</i>

1065
01:04:39,564 --> 01:04:41,107
<i>I miss you.</i>

1066
01:04:49,491 --> 01:04:50,366
2002 TO 2003

1067
01:04:56,873 --> 01:04:58,625
<i>Her belly is cold.</i>

1068
01:04:58,708 --> 01:05:01,336
<i>I'm worried because</i>
<i>she always has a stomachache.</i>

1069
01:05:02,295 --> 01:05:05,465
<i>I should brew</i>
<i>some herbal medicine for her.</i>

1070
01:05:08,259 --> 01:05:10,178
Grandma.

1071
01:05:10,261 --> 01:05:13,014
My tummy aches. Can I have a tummy rub?

1072
01:05:13,097 --> 01:05:14,807
Do you have a stomachache again?

1073
01:05:14,891 --> 01:05:15,934
Come here.

1074
01:05:16,518 --> 01:05:17,769
Oh my.

1075
01:05:17,852 --> 01:05:19,771
Grandma will give you her healing hands.

1076
01:05:19,854 --> 01:05:24,442
<i>Grandma's hands are healing hands</i>

1077
01:05:24,526 --> 01:05:27,820
<i>Seo-ri's tummy is a potbelly</i>

1078
01:05:27,904 --> 01:05:30,281
Hey! I don't have a potbelly!

1079
01:05:31,950 --> 01:05:36,120
<i>Grandma's hands are healing hands</i>

1080
01:05:36,704 --> 01:05:40,500
<i>Seo-ri's tummy is a potbelly</i>

1081
01:05:44,921 --> 01:05:46,130
<i>What is this?</i>

1082
01:05:48,800 --> 01:05:51,427
<i>They told me to wait.</i>

1083
01:05:53,805 --> 01:05:56,391
<i>They said they'd be right back.</i>

1084
01:05:58,935 --> 01:06:01,813
<i>They told me to wait here.</i>

1085
01:06:02,814 --> 01:06:04,148
What is wrong with me?

1086
01:06:05,108 --> 01:06:06,651
<i>But that's quite strange.</i>

1087
01:06:06,734 --> 01:06:09,529
<i>Childhood memories</i>
<i>should have been borne away</i>

1088
01:06:09,612 --> 01:06:10,989
<i>with the soul of the body's master.</i>

1089
01:06:11,072 --> 01:06:13,283
<i>How did they stay and get tangled up?</i>

1090
01:06:13,366 --> 01:06:15,535
Why do I keep…

1091
01:06:19,706 --> 01:06:23,251
<i>Right. This is not my body,</i>
<i>and those are not my memories.</i>

1092
01:06:24,002 --> 01:06:25,503
<i>How did they get tangled with my own?</i>

1093
01:06:25,587 --> 01:06:27,255
<i>I was just trapped again.</i>

1094
01:06:27,338 --> 01:06:28,756
<i>I was trapped.</i>

1095
01:06:28,840 --> 01:06:30,633
It felt like I was dying.

1096
01:06:31,551 --> 01:06:33,803
<i>The soul and memories are a pair.</i>

1097
01:06:33,886 --> 01:06:35,930
<i>They shouldn't be separated.</i>

1098
01:06:36,723 --> 01:06:38,266
<i>It feels like they are mine.</i>

1099
01:06:40,560 --> 01:06:42,145
<i>How does that make sense?</i>

1100
01:06:45,148 --> 01:06:46,149
<i>How?</i>

1101
01:06:47,108 --> 01:06:47,984
<i>Seo-ri.</i>

1102
01:06:50,194 --> 01:06:51,571
My sweet girl.

1103
01:06:52,905 --> 01:06:54,407
My sweet girl.

1104
01:06:56,743 --> 01:06:58,202
My sweet girl.

1105
01:06:58,911 --> 01:07:00,246
When are you coming?

1106
01:07:00,830 --> 01:07:04,667
<i>When is my sweet girl coming?</i>

1107
01:07:19,849 --> 01:07:21,267
<i>Seo-ri.</i>

1108
01:07:21,893 --> 01:07:23,269
<i>My sweet girl.</i>

1109
01:07:25,313 --> 01:07:26,606
Grandma!

1110
01:07:26,689 --> 01:07:27,774
Grandma.

1111
01:07:38,326 --> 01:07:41,954
<i>Seo-ri, my sweet girl.</i>

1112
01:07:42,038 --> 01:07:43,206
Grandma!

1113
01:07:44,374 --> 01:07:46,376
-Grandma, I'll be taller than you!
-Yeah.

1114
01:07:46,459 --> 01:07:47,335
Okay, let's make sure!

1115
01:07:47,418 --> 01:07:49,003
My sweet girl.

1116
01:07:49,087 --> 01:07:50,797
This is crazy!

1117
01:07:50,880 --> 01:07:51,798
Really?

1118
01:07:51,881 --> 01:07:54,384
My sweet girl. How exciting!

1119
01:07:56,052 --> 01:07:57,136
My sweet girl.

1120
01:08:00,515 --> 01:08:02,266
My sweet girl.

1121
01:08:11,025 --> 01:08:12,360
<i>Grandma.</i>

1122
01:08:23,162 --> 01:08:24,455
<i>That's not you.</i>

1123
01:08:26,332 --> 01:08:27,583
<i>You're just a fake.</i>

1124
01:08:27,667 --> 01:08:29,460
<i>Get out of my body.</i>

1125
01:08:31,629 --> 01:08:34,006
<i>No, I am not a fake.</i>

1126
01:08:35,550 --> 01:08:36,509
<i>I am…</i>

1127
01:08:37,427 --> 01:08:38,511
<i>My name is…</i>

1128
01:08:44,809 --> 01:08:45,852
<i>Shin Seo-ri.</i>

1129
01:09:20,678 --> 01:09:21,763
Just a little bit.

1130
01:09:24,056 --> 01:09:25,349
Just wait a little bit longer.

1131
01:09:50,666 --> 01:09:54,253
MY ROYAL NEMESIS

1132
01:10:24,865 --> 01:10:26,160
I'm not letting you go anywhere.

1133
01:10:26,244 --> 01:10:27,537
<i>I am not going back.</i>

1134
01:10:27,620 --> 01:10:30,039
<i>Because I have returned to where I belong.</i>

1135
01:10:30,122 --> 01:10:32,054
I'll put the brakes
on the resort development.

1136
01:10:32,133 --> 01:10:34,418
I hear they're building an airport
next to the resort site.

1137
01:10:34,502 --> 01:10:36,754
<i>-What about Seo-jun?</i>
<i>-Your driver picked him up.</i>

1138
01:10:36,838 --> 01:10:38,756
<i>Your threat was loud and clear.</i>

1139
01:10:38,840 --> 01:10:40,883
And you crossed a line you shouldn't have.

1140
01:10:40,967 --> 01:10:43,427
<i>Her condition has rapidly deteriorated.</i>

1141
01:10:44,554 --> 01:10:45,471
<i>Grandma.</i>

1142
01:10:45,555 --> 01:10:47,223
<i>Tell me.</i>

1143
01:10:47,306 --> 01:10:48,808
I will pay any price!

1144
01:10:48,891 --> 01:10:52,270
<i>Even at the cost</i>
<i>of never returning here again?</i>

1145
01:10:55,275 --> 01:10:57,275
Subtitle translation by Justin S. Kim

